menuconfig RTSP_SERVER
    bool "RTSP Server (MJPEG streaming)"
    depends on COMPONENTS_LWIP_ENABLE
    default n
    help
      Enable RTSP server for MJPEG/H.264 streaming over lwIP on
      FreeRTOS (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt).

      Pull-model frame source: producer registers a get_frm_t callback
      via set_strm_cb(); RTSP session pulls frames at the configured
      fps. ISP integration (Phase 5) just wires the ISP JPEG-done
      path into the same callback.

if RTSP_SERVER

config RTSP_LISTEN_PORT
    int "RTSP listen port"
    default 8554
    range 1 65535
    help
      TCP port for RTSP control channel. Default 8554 matches the
      library's DFL_RTSP_PORT. Use 554 only if you also own the
      privileged-port capability on your network.

config RTSP_DEFAULT_VIDEO_FPS
    int "Default video fps"
    default 5
    range 1 60
    help
      Default frame rate for the pull-model source. Phase 4 test
      source uses this to pace its canned-frame rotation.

config RTSP_TASK_STACK_SIZE
    int "RTSP listener task stack (bytes)"
    default 4096
    range 2048 16384
    help
      Stack size for the main RTSP server task (rtsp_srv_thrd).
      Per-session tasks reuse the same default. Bump to 6144 if
      stack-overflow assertions fire during long soaks.

config RTSP_TEST_SOURCE
    bool "Compile Phase 4 canned-frame test source"
    default y
    help
      When enabled, builds rtsp_test_source.c which implements a
      get_frm_t callback that cycles through canned JPEG frames from
      apps/platform/ipro7_demo/demo/esp32_at/mjpeg_frames.h (or an
      embedded fallback 720p JPEG). Turn OFF in Phase 5 when the
      real ISP callback is wired in.

config RTSP_ISP_SOURCE
    bool "Compile Phase 5 ISP -> MJPEG real source"
    depends on MM_SUPPORT && COMPONENTS_SENSOR_ENABLE
    default y if MM_SUPPORT
    help
      When enabled, builds rtsp_isp_source.c which boots the IPRO7
      sensor + ISP + MJPEG pipeline and serves real-time JPEG frames
      to the RTSP server through a get_frm_t callback. Mutually
      exclusive at runtime with RTSP_TEST_SOURCE — install one or
      the other via the shell (rtsp_isp_src on / rtsp_test_src on).

config RTSP_SHELL
    bool "Enable dev shell commands (rtsp_*)"
    default y

config RTSP_AUTOSTART
    bool "Auto-start RTSP server when host netif has IP"
    depends on ESP_HOSTED_NETIF
    default y
    help
      Spawn a task during app_main that polls
      esp_hosted_netif_is_ip_ready() and calls rtsp_init_lib() +
      rtsp_test_source_install() (if enabled) once the host has a
      DHCP lease. Requires the user to drive eh_init + eh_connect
      from the shell; this only automates what happens AFTER IP is
      up. Turn OFF to drive the full sequence manually.

endif # RTSP_SERVER
